      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1939e94c-3403-516e-b74c-50652e3a0788",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gertrude Stein, Pablo Picasso\n- Works: If I Told Him: A Completed Portrait of Picasso, Portraits and Prayers\n- Publications: Vanity Fair\n- Places: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, Oakland, California, Paris, France\n- Topics: writing, publication, biography\n\nFacts:\n- Gertrude Stein was born on February 3, 1874, in the Allegheny West neighborhood of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n- Gertrude Stein was raised in Oakland, California.\n- Gertrude Stein moved to Paris in 1903 and made France her home for the rest of her life.\n- Gertrude Stein wrote \"If I Told Him: A Completed Portrait of Picasso\" in 1923.\n- \"If I Told Him: A Completed Portrait of Picasso\" was first published in Vanity Fair in 1924.\n- Gertrude Stein later republished \"If I Told Him: A Completed Portrait of Picasso\" in her collection \"Portraits and Prayers\".\n- Gertrude Stein was an American novelist, poet, playwright, and art collector.\n- Gertrude Stein died on July 27, 1946.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
